WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.350
Here's how to feel a game's DualSense haptics on a controller that only rumbles.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.670
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:13.365
This PlayStation controller has an Xbox Series X Controller assigned.

4
00:00:13.935 --> 00:00:14.565
Open it.

5
00:00:15.035 --> 00:00:18.725
Its preset is DualSense (PS5): Full, the default,

6
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:21.145
and the one that carries a game's haptics.

7
00:00:22.375 --> 00:00:27.445
Games that use the DualSense's haptics play them as sound, and send no rumble.

8
00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:34.395
PadForge turns that sound's loudness into rumble on the Xbox pad: the left channel drives the left motor,

9
00:00:34.435 --> 00:00:36.305
and the right channel the right.

10
00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:43.644
On the Force Feedback tab, Overall Gain sets how strong it feels.

11
00:00:44.454 --> 00:00:45.884
Zero turns it off for this pad.

12
00:00:47.159 --> 00:00:48.729
There's nothing else to set.

13
00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:50.549
No game ran for this video.

14
00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:55.522
Find more guides at padforge.org.
